# CHANGELOG.md uses git's `union` merge driver: when two branches both add
# lines to the same section (typical for the auto-changelog bot when several
# issues close close together), git keeps BOTH sides' additions instead of
# emitting <<<<<<< / ======= / >>>>>>> conflict markers. Order between the
# two sets of new lines is non-deterministic and can be tidied later; the
# important thing is that merges never fail on this file. Refs #17.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
